# Flame Detection and Tracking System Using ESP32

## Overview

This project is an ESP32-based Flame Detection and Tracking System that detects fire using an IR flame sensor, tracks the flame direction with servo motors, and sends real-time notifications through the Blynk IoT platform. A relay-controlled water pump is activated automatically to help extinguish the detected flame.

## Features

* Flame detection using IR flame sensor
* Automatic flame tracking with servo motors
* Real-time fire alerts via Blynk IoT
* Automatic water pump activation
* ESP32 Wi-Fi connectivity
* Low-cost fire safety solution

## Hardware Components

* ESP32 Development Board
* IR Flame Sensor
* 2 × SG90 Servo Motors
* Relay Module
* Water Pump
* Buck Converter
* Lithium-Ion Battery
* Jumper Wires

## Software

* Arduino IDE
* ESP32 Board Package
* Blynk IoT
* C++

## Pin Configuration

| Component    | ESP32 Pin |
| ------------ | --------- |
| Flame Sensor | GPIO 27   |
| Relay Module | GPIO 23   |
| Sensor Servo | GPIO 18   |
| Pump Servo   | GPIO 19   |

## Working

1. The servo-mounted flame sensor continuously scans the area.
2. When a flame is detected, the system identifies its direction.
3. The pump nozzle aligns with the detected flame.
4. A Blynk notification is sent to the user.
5. The relay activates the water pump to suppress the fire.
6. The system continues spraying until the flame is no longer detected.

## Applications

* Home Fire Safety
* Smart Buildings
* Industrial Monitoring
* Laboratories and Workshops
* IoT-Based Safety Systems

